pkg:Evidence_v1_1_1 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.1.1 (PATCH release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "PATCH: documentation-only addition, no ontology/gate content change to the four-stage artifacts. Adds 00-proposals/Handover_RDODI_Template_Drift_v1_0_0.md, filed after the user reported the Stage 4 page does not match an expected sidebar-tree/sub-tabs/grounded-prompt template. Investigation verified: (1) the DOCX companion added in v1.1.0 is genuinely on GitHub -- fetched directly via raw.githubusercontent.com, HTTP 200, SHA-256 matches the local file byte-for-byte; the reported inaccessibility is most likely GitHub's lack of an inline .docx preview, not a push failure. (2) No shipped RDODI artifact -- not the procedure, not ch10 v1-v4, not rdodi_presentation_renderer_v1_0_0.py, not either presentation-samples output, not kb_explorer -- implements sub-tabs or a hierarchical sidebar tree; all are single flowing pages with anchor-based in-page navigation. The interactive-page ontology declares real but entirely unconsumed vocabulary for that richer pattern (ipo:SubPageTabs, ipo:PageHierarchy, ipo:LandingPageVariant) -- grepped end to end, zero consumers in procedure, gates, renderer, or worked examples. The feature set the user described (collapsible tree sidebar, sub-tabs, a live-LLM-grounded prompt console) exists verbatim in a separate, unrelated package -- lcw-principles-kb/04-page/lcw_kb_interactive_v0_92_0.html -- built under a different commission with no cross-reference from any RDODI document. Handover returns two options to the RDODI session (B1, package-owner decision, not made here): adopt the richer pattern as RDODI's real Stage 4 standard and build a consuming renderer, or document the single-page boundary explicitly and mark the unused vocabulary as aspirational."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "95b3d2e0829a534032b7212bc14f5702bf5215f37d142080fe3ee9258023708f"^^xsd:string .
